	quest.0EF472D138711500.quest_subtitle: "can you have a frog in a bucket too"
	quest.0F35AF004588B678.quest_subtitle: "The thing your train goes on. No tracks, no train."
	quest.0F35AF004588B678.title: "Train Tracks"
	quest.0F9CC22264DF80E8.quest_subtitle: "When powered, extends a redstone pulse for a specified time, much like a Redstone Repeater. The time can be set in its Value Settings Screen accessed by holding right-click. It can be set to extend a signal for 2 ticks up to 60 minutes. The settings can also be copied and pasted onto other extenders or Pulse Repeaters by using a Clipboard."
	quest.0FB4FFD361C5DF69.quest_subtitle: "It's just a seat, nothing more, nothing less. But if you're in a moving contraption, might as well glue it to the contraption so you can sit and move along with it. Don't superglue yourself to the seat."
	quest.0FB4FFD361C5DF69.title: "Chair."
	quest.0FBB5A02F560CAB9.quest_subtitle: "The Analog Lever is used to emit a variable signal."
	quest.0FCB25BA5EB5E745.quest_subtitle: "Chains together individual Minecarts, causing them to move as a group"
	quest.0FF39255BD5908AD.title: "Crush Nether Wart to obtain Spices"
	quest.0FFF02638951EBAE.quest_desc: ["Craft a canvas rug by putting a piece of canvas in the crafting table. "]
	quest.0FFF02638951EBAE.title: "Your life is your canvas (rug)..."
	quest.10331210B10CF626.quest_subtitle: "Lets you use SU to break blocks, can also be attached to contraptions to make tunnel bores and the like."
	quest.10622C9E74C50A95.quest_subtitle: "Seats are used to allow multiple entities to ride a Contraption. Seats come in every color of Dye. They function much like a Boat in that they can be ridden by players and mobs"
	quest.10F1FE4B7907DF37.quest_subtitle: "The Smart Observer is a machine that emits a redstone signal dependent on the block or items inside a container in front of it."
	quest.111C3069CE77EFF2.quest_subtitle: "Attribute filters focus only on data. The filter can Allow items with any of the desired attributes, only allow them if they have all of the desired attributes, or deny items with any of the selected attributes. A reference item is required to show and choose attributes, but attributes can be added by multiple items."
